= Cryptocurrency wallet =

== Overview ==
'''Cryptocurrency wallet''' is hardware, software, or a service that generates, stores, manages, or uses cryptographic keys and addresses needed to authorize interactions with cryptocurrency or blockchain systems.

Wallets typically do not contain the blockchain assets themselves. Assets are represented by ledger state; the wallet holds or accesses the credentials needed to authorize state changes.

Wallet architectures include self-custodial, externally hosted, multi-signature, smart-contract, hardware, software, and hybrid designs. Recovery and security assumptions differ across these models.

Loss or compromise of private keys can cause loss of control unless the account or wallet design includes recovery, social authorization, key rotation, or another mechanism.

== Boundaries ==
* wallet ≠ storage location of coins on the ledger
* wallet ≠ private key only
* self-custody ≠ automatic security

